# Essential Modules for DevOps Engineers

| Module   | Purpose                                   |
| -------- | ----------------------------------------- |
| package  | Install or remove packages                |
| service  | Start, stop, restart services             |
| copy     | Copy files                                |
| template | Deploy dynamic configuration files        |
| file     | Manage files and directories              |
| command  | Run commands                              |
| shell    | Run shell commands with pipes/redirection |
| user     | Manage users                              |
| reboot   | Reboot servers                            |
| get_url  | Download files                            |
| uri      | Call REST APIs                            |
| git      | Clone repositories                        |
| cron     | Manage scheduled jobs                     |
| systemd  | Manage systemd services                   |

---

# Recommended Learning Order

1. debug
2. package
3. service
4. copy
5. file
6. command
7. shell
8. user
9. reboot
10. template

These modules cover most day-to-day DevOps automation tasks and provide a strong foundation for learning advanced Ansible concepts such as Roles, Handlers, Vault, Dynamic Inventory, and Collections.
